ertification Framework','2025-05-15 22:17:15'),(999,'Emission Trading Scheme','2025-05-15 22:17:15'),(1000,'Based on our vast experience in Italian and EU cultural heritage regulation, we plan to contribute to the EU’s role to assist and complement the actions of Member States in preserving and promoting Europe\'s cultural heritage','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1001,'Our Association has been pursuing a dialogue with the Italian institutions aimed at facilitating the circulation of art (and, consequently of knowledge and culture) within the European territory','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1002,'For example, we have been in constant dialogue with the Italian parliament members and policy makers to assess whether the cumbersome and bureaucratic control exercised by the Italian export offices on the international circulation of art (into and out of the Italian territory) is the most efficient way to protect the European cultural heritage','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1003,'We believe that an over-protective and over-controlling system has the deterrent effect of preventing foreign and Italian collectors from shipping their artworks to Italy or making them publicly available with loans to public museums At the same time, also the fruition of Italian art by European citizens may be hindered due to a lengthy domestic export system guided by uncertain and overly discretional principles We would like to refer to our 2022 position paper  https://wwwgruppoapolloit/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/4_Apollo_position-paper_stampa_A4pdf','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1004,'We are planning to bring these issues to the attention of the European Institutions (EU Parliament and Commission) also in light of the Council Resolution on the Workplan for Culture 2023/2026 (2022/C 466/01)','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1005,'In particular, we believe that a better circulation of art within Europe is consistent with the following Guiding Principles (Annex I) of the above-mentioned Resolution:','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1006,'-	Culture, including cultural heritage, has an intrinsic value and contributes to strengthening European identity','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1007,'-	Cultural and linguistic diversity are fundamental assets of the EU and are to be respected, promoted and enhanced, including through mobility and the circulation of works (emphasys added)','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1008,'-	Freedom of artistic expression and creativity are fundamental to the human ability to address challenges, to think critically, to innovate and to invent, and they must be encouraged and supported in all relevant ways','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1009,'-	Cultural diversity and intercultural dialogue are essential for the promotion and protection of human rights they foster mutual understanding, help prevent and resolve conflicts and promote reconciliation, peace and international stability, and any misuse of culture with the aim of spreading war propaganda and disinformation and of instigating hatred is incompatible with the fundamental values and principles of the EU','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1010,'-	Culture makes a significant contribution to sustainable development, the economy and social inclusion, enhancing territorial cohesion','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1011,'-	Culture has the potential to promote equality and mutual respect, and to fight against all forms of violence, discrimination, intolerance and prejudice','2025-05-15 22:17:16'),(1012,'Propuestas legislativas o políticas de la UE relacionadas con los objetivos de nuestra institución, entre otros I+D+i (Programa Horizonte Europa, Life, RFCS, Interreg) y educación superior (Erasmus+) En concreto, políticas relacionadas con las prioridades del entorno regional, como la política de transición justa, descarbonización, pacto verde, economía circular, digitalización, etc','2025-05-15 22:17:17'),(1013,'Ibex Publishing\'s strategic communications consultancy services are designed to provide advisory support to corporate entities and non-corporate clients regarding optimal engagement strategies with governmental and public institutions on matters of policy, legislation, and regulation pertinent to their interests The specific European Union legislative proposals and/or policies under scrutiny are subject to the particular interests of our clientele however, they encompass initiatives such as ReFuelEU Aviation, FuelEU Maritime, the EU Emissions Trading Scheme (ETS), the trans-European transport network (TEN-T), and CO2 emission performance standards for cars and vans','2025-05-15 22:17:17'),(1014,'Clean Sky','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1015,'SESAR','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1016,'EASA','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1017,'Aviation package','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1018,'Energy Union','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1019,'Strategic Transport Research and Innovation Agenda','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1020,'Clean Aviation','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1021,'Single European Sky ATM Research','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1022,'SBA','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1023,'Technology Infrastructures','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1024,'Drone Strategy','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1025,'RefuelEU','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1026,'EDF','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1027,'Sustainable and Smart Mobility Strategy','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1028,'EU 2016/2102','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1029,'EN 301 549','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1030,'VN verdrag inzake de rechten van personen met een handicap','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1031,'DIRECTIVE (EU) 2019/882 Accesibility Act','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1032,'Implementatiewet Toegankelijkheid','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1033,'The European Accessibility Act (Directive 2019/882)','2025-05-15 22:17:18'),(1034,'BHP is interested in following developments related to the EU Critical Raw Materials Act','2025-05-15 22:17:19'),(1035,'Programme de travail Horizon Europe','2025-05-15 22:17:20'),(1036,'Programme de travail EU4Health','2025-05-15 22:17:20'),(1037,'Implementation de la Directive 2010/63/EU2 on the protection of animals used for scientific purpose','2025-05-15 22:17:20'),(10