aving clinical, financial and operational outcomes in mind Always with the focus of Mobility','2025-05-15 22:18:08'),(1367,'The Clean Industrial Deal, Circular Economy Act, ELVR, Chemicals Industry Package including REACH,  Industrial Action Plan for the Automotive Sector, Energy & Climate Policy, Innovation & Research, Health & Environmental Policy, Chemicals Policy, Trade and Competition Policy, Industrial Policy','2025-05-15 22:18:09'),(1368,'The proposed Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD) This proposed Directive will set out a horizontal framework to foster the contribution of businesses operating in the single market to the respect of the human rights and environment in their own operations and through their value chains, by identifying, preventing, mitigating and accounting for their adverse human rights, and environmental impacts, and having adequate governance, management systems and measures in place to this end','2025-05-15 22:18:09'),(1369,'Sustainable finance','2025-05-15 22:18:09'),(1370,'A Commission workstream that supports the European green deal aim of channelling private investment towards the transition to a climate-neutral economy Amongst others focusing on the EU taxonomy for sustainable activities and the Corporate disclosure of climate-related information','2025-05-15 22:18:09'),(1371,'The EU Space Programme','2025-05-15 22:18:10'),(1372,'Programme duration: 2021-2027','2025-05-15 22:18:10'),(1373,'Lead Directorate-General: Defence Industry and Space (DEFIS), which is the Commission department responsible for EU policy on defence industry and space, leading the European Commission\'s activities in the Defence Industry and Space sector','2025-05-15 22:18:10'),(1374,'https://eceuropaeu/info/funding-tenders/find-funding/eu-funding-programmes/european-space-programme_en','2025-05-15 22:18:10'),(1375,'EMA advocates for a metropolitan dimension in EU policies Since 2015, EMA has been debating and working on Cohesion Policy, the European Green Deal, Jobs and Social Rights, Sustainable Mobility and Transport, and the Multiannual Financial Framework','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1376,'In February 2020, a delegation of EMA political representatives met with Commissioner Elisa Ferreira to discuss the future of Cohesion Policy, the European Urban Agenda, and their metropolitan dimension and impacts An EMA delegation also met with Commissioner Corina Crețu in 2017 Additionally, EMA has participated in various meetings of the URBAN Intergroup of the European Parliament','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1377,'In previous editions of the EMA annual conferences, we have welcomed representatives from the European Parliament, the European Commission, and the Committee of the Regions','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1378,'The last EMA Forum, held in Amsterdam (Netherlands) in 2024, gathered more than 90 participants from 25 cities, metropolitan areas, and regions The forum also welcomed several Members of the European Parliament, along with Nicola De Michelis, Acting Deputy Director-General for Regional and Urban Policy at the European Commission','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1379,'In 2024, EMA also participated in the high-level conference \"An Appropriate European Urban Policy for the Future,\" organized under the auspices of the Belgian Presidency of the European Union','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1380,'We work toward a full implementation of the EU FORB Guidelines policies about freedom of religion and belief','2025-05-15 22:18:11'),(1381,'Politici sociale sanatate si securitate la locul de munca','2025-05-15 22:18:12'),(1382,'Reprezentarea salariatilor','2025-05-15 22:18:12'),(1383,'Promovarea si apararea drepturilor salariatilor','2025-05-15 22:18:12'),(1384,'Dezvoltare economica si ocupare','2025-05-15 22:18:12'),(1385,'Educatia adultilor','2025-05-15 22:18:12'),(1386,'Gesetzesvorhaben und Konsultationen in den Bereichen: Außen- und Sicherheitspolitik, Binnenmarkt, Handel, Beschäftigung und Soziales, Energie, Bildung, Forschu